      <p class="pt">Two tool defects showed. First, the batch script told workers that the count stage, the run that measures the count, takes 20 seconds, and ran it in the foreground. Since batch 13b it takes about 5 minutes. One worker's run passed the shell tool's 5-minute limit, and another cut its run and started it again. After the landing the script was fixed: it gives the measured times and starts the count in the background.</p>
      <p class="pt">Second, the measuring script counted a build only when a command started with <code>ant</code>, but workers now build through <code>nohup bash -c</code>, as the skill says. So it read 0 builds for this batch's workers, where the transcripts show 6. It now counts both forms: 6 for this batch, and 11 for batch 13.</p>
      <p class="pt">After the landing, the record caught up. The skill writer rewrote the five skill sentences that the batch made false, and widened one more. The record pass cut twelve FACTS entries to the record's form, and POSITIONS marked three of your decisions built. PLAN took the batch's line, batch 15's candidates and your list.</p>
