<div class="wrap">
  <header class="top">
    <h1>Batch 15 Landed</h1>
    <p class="deck">Climb batch 15's final report: whether it landed, what it changed in Fortress, what it cost from preparation to landing, how the work went, what's for your review, and what comes next.</p>
    <p class="stamp">14 Oct 2026, 16:19 UTC (18:19 yours) · landed at c40489978 · review at d8a98c515</p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-answer">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="h-answer">The answer</h2>
      <button class="select" type="button" data-target="s-answer" aria-label="Select the text of this section">Select</button>
    </div>
    <div class="speak" id="s-answer">
      <p class="pt">Yes. All four fixes landed on main at 15:55 UTC today (17:55 yours). Every skeptic approved its fix, none of their own edits was contested, and no judge or repair round was needed.</p>
      <p class="pt">The gate was green: 2.0K fast tests, 621 system tests and 130 specification examples, with no failure. microGPT's two quick checks under walk passed 7 of 7 each.</p>
      <p class="pt">The distance went from 54 to 49, exactly as planned. The count stayed at 1, but its one error moved. Walk now lets the library type <code>body(i)</code>, so the count stops at the next error: row 680's crash in <code>Array3</code>, the rank-3 array trait.</p>
      <p class="pt">The fix for that crash was built and works, but it's held. With it in, the count stage checks the library's main component whole for the first time: 43 errors in 809 seconds. That's past the 690-second line the batch set to keep the stage clear of its 900-second cut-off, since a run past the cut-off turns the gate red. So the fix waits, and it's the first item for you.</p>
      <p class="pt">The run wrote 4.44M tokens in 5 h 03 min, with 12 agents. With its preparation and landing, the batch cost about 8.9M.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Sources</h3>
      <p><b>1.</b> The landing commit <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/c40489978">c40489978</a>; the four fixes' commits: the gather's <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/compile-ladder/climb-batch-15/RECORD.md">RECORD.md</a>, &ldquo;The landed commits&rdquo;.</p>
      <p><b>2.</b> <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/compile-ladder/climb-batch-15/gate/summary.txt">gate/summary.txt</a>: testFast 1,984 tests, testSystem 621, testSpecData 130, 42 of 42 atomic runs; the commit's message for microGPT's two &ldquo;7 PASS, 0 FAIL of 7&rdquo;.</p>
      <p><b>3.</b> <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/compile-ladder/climb-batch-15/gate/distance.txt">gate/distance.txt</a> (&ldquo;#total 49&rdquo;) and <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/compile-ladder/climb-batch-15/gate/checker-count.txt">gate/checker-count.txt</a> (&ldquo;#total 1&rdquo;).</p>
      <p><b>4.</b> The held fix's measurement: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/compile-ladder/rung-checker-bounds/REPORT.md">rung-checker-bounds/REPORT.md</a>, section 6, run 2.</p>
      <p><b>5.</b> The cost: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/reviews/batch-15-review.md">batch-15-review.md</a>, the cost section, by the coordinator's <code>spend.py</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-fortress">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="h-fortress">What changed in Fortress</h2>
      <button class="select" type="button" data-target="s-fortress" aria-label="Select the text of this section">Select</button>
    </div>
    <div class="speak" id="s-fortress">
      <p class="pt"><b>Walk types a reduction or a comprehension that writes no static argument.</b> In <code>xs: List[\ZZ32\] = &lt;| k | k &lt;- 0#3 |&gt;</code> nothing written fixes the list's element type. Walk used to give it the empty type, so the result was refused at the binding. Now walk takes the type declared for the value, here <code>ZZ32</code>; without one, the common type of the elements it computes; without elements, the parameter's bound, as your P-48 asks. So the library's big-operator function types its <code>body(i)</code> at last, and three tests that recorded the old gap now pass. microGPT writes every static argument, so it's untouched.</p>
      <p class="pt"><b>The checker handles a parameter bounded by a closed trait and another trait.</b> The vectors and matrices take <code>T extends { Number, MultiplicativeRing[\T\] }</code>, and <code>Number</code> lists its cases in a <code>comprises</code> clause. The checker used to replace <code>Number</code> by those cases even inside such a bound, so calls through <code>T</code> were refused or crashed it. Now it expands a closed trait only against a type with no type variable in it, so the library's <code>squaredNorm(me)</code>, two call shapes that crashed the checker and one overloading it wrongly refused now check, compile and run.</p>
      <p class="pt"><b>The vector and matrix factories choose their store per number type.</b> <code>array1</code> and <code>array2</code> now pick a vector or a matrix by a <code>typecase</code> on the type they return, then <code>cast</code>, as <code>additiveIdentity</code> already did. That cleared 4 errors. At a type that isn't one of the eight number types, such as <code>Number</code> itself, they now give a plain array, whose <code>+</code> doesn't run. That includes walk's case where the element type is guessed from <code>ZZ32</code> values, so write the static argument there.</p>
      <p class="pt"><b><code>IntMap</code>'s disjoint union throws on a shared key.</b> <code>{1 |-&gt; 1} UPLUS {1 |-&gt; 9}</code> now throws <code>KeyOverlap</code> in either order, by the library's own <code>addNew</code>. Before, one of the two orders quietly kept one of the values.</p>
      <p class="pt"><b>The No Duplicates Rule and coverage, on both paths.</b> The checker now refuses two functional methods whose parameter types match wherever their <code>self</code> parameters stand. It also finds an inherited abstract method covered through the cases <code>comprises</code> clauses list. Walk now refuses an object when its search for such a cover can't settle, where it used to let it through. No error moved; six new gaps went into the ledger.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Sources</h3>
      <p><b>1.</b> Commit <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/20474c144">20474c144</a>; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-elements/REPORT.md">rung-walk-elements/REPORT.md</a>; the old refusal: the gather's record, &ldquo;Rung B&rdquo;'s recorded failure; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/ProjectFortress/tests/UnwrittenComprehensionDeclaredTypeWalk.fss">tests/UnwrittenComprehensionDeclaredTypeWalk.fss</a>.</p>
      <p><b>2.</b> Commit <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/f237148ac">f237148ac</a>; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/compile-ladder/rung-checker-bounds/REPORT.md">rung-checker-bounds/REPORT.md</a>, section 1.</p>
      <p><b>3.</b> Commit <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/a0f839ad7">a0f839ad7</a>; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/ProjectFortress/tests/ArrayFactoryAbstractNumber.fss">tests/ArrayFactoryAbstractNumber.fss</a>; ledger row 721.</p>
      <p><b>4.</b> The same commit; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/ProjectFortress/tests/IntMapUplusSingleton.fss">tests/IntMapUplusSingleton.fss</a>, lines 24 and 25.</p>
      <p><b>5.</b> Commit <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/59b1d0a4d">59b1d0a4d</a>; ledger rows 707 to 709 closed, 723 to 728 opened.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-cost">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="h-cost">The cost, from preparation to landing</h2>
